WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:04.330
- [Narrator] This is S.J. -
a prehensile tailed skink.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:06.480
Found in the Solomon Islands,

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.643
this little guy is the
largest known of its kind.

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:18.600
The prehensile-tailed skink's
body is a greenish olive color

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.501
with scattered black scales.

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:23.480
This coloring, combined
with its slow movements,

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.870
helps the skink to camouflage
with its surroundings

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:27.576
and hide from enemies.

00:00:27.576 --> 00:00:32.140
Like other skinks, its head
is flat and triangular.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.390
Their strong legs and sharp
claws help them to climb trees.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:39.760
The defining feature on this
skink is its prehensile tail,

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.680
which allows them to grasp
objects and branches for balance.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.513
Their tail makes up nearly
half of their bodies length.

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:52.240
The prehensile-tailed skink's
habitat is under threat

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:55.660
due to deforestation for
lumber and agriculture.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:58.470
This and the skink's
popularity within the pet trade

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.633
has threatened their survival in the wild.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.273
This is the prehensile-tailed skink.

